# pkglist.aur --- the stuff even the repos wouldn't take -*- mode: conf -*-
#
# Apply on a fresh machine with:
#   yay -S --needed - < packages/gengar/pkglist.aur
#
# This file is hand-curated -- edit it by hand. DO NOT `pacman -Qqem >` over it;
# that re-sorts, drops the comments, and murders every joke below. To spot drift
# between this file and what's actually installed (comments/order ignored), run:
#   yay-drift               # '-' = in here only, '+' = installed only
# (a script in shell/.local/bin/)
#
# Rule 1: repos first, AUR only when the repos can't or won't. Everything below
# is here because it lost that argument -- an AUR helper (yay/paru) builds these
# from source, so keep them out of the pacman list or its apply will choke.
#
# Rule 2: see Rule 1.

# browsers
google-chrome                                  # the RAM goes where, exactly?

# editors / IDEs
visual-studio-code-bin                         # the electron app that ate the world

# terminals
tilix                                          # tiling terminal, gtk flavored

# desktop bits
nitrogen                                       # feh with a mouse for the wallpaper
simplescreenrecorder                           # captures the screen, name says the rest

# gaming
heroic-games-launcher-bin                      # epic + gog, minus the epic launcher

# shell / cli utilities
gnu-netcat                                     # reads and writes sockets (openbsd-netcat if you need v6)
